Hi quranpedia team,

I'm the maintainer of open-mushaf-native, an open-source Quran reader
app for iOS, Android, and Web (https://github.com/adelpro/open-mushaf-native).
It currently serves two mushafs (Hafs and Warsh from Medina Mushaf)
as raster PNGs bundled into the install package.

I'm planning a migration to vector SVG rendering using your
quranpedia/quran-svg repository, which provides both the SVG pages and
polygon-based hit-regions for true ayah selection. This is a much
better technical fit than the raster approach.

What I would like permission to do:

1. Bundle (include in the install package) the Hafs and Warsh KFQC
   pages from your repo, pinned to a specific commit SHA.

2. At runtime, fetch the other four mushafs (Qalun-KFQC, Qalun-Libya,
   Douri-KFQC, Shubah-KFQC) over the jsDelivr CDN from the same repo,
   when a user chooses to download them. No redistribution to other
   servers — the files are pulled straight from GitHub via jsDelivr's
   edge cache, exactly as a browser would.

3. Display the SVG pages and let users tap on ayahs (your polygon
   data) to open a tafseer.

The app is free, ad-free, and donation-supported. It is already
published on the App Store (id 6783070437) and Play Store
(com.adelpro.openmushafnative). Total installs: small but growing.

Could you confirm in writing (a reply to this email is fine) that:

- Bundling the Hafs and Warsh SVG pages in our APK is OK.
- Fetching the other four mushafs from your repo at runtime via
  jsDelivr is OK.
- Citing quranpedia/quran-svg as the source in our app's "About"
  screen is acceptable.

I am happy to:
- Credit quranpedia prominently in the app's About screen and on
  the GitHub README.
- Link to your website (https://quranpedia.net) from the app.
- Not modify the SVG files in any way.
- Pin to a specific commit SHA and not auto-update.

Thank you for the work you put into this repo — it solves a real
problem for Quran apps that previously had to ship raster scans of
the mushaf.

Best,
Adel Benyahia

